      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSika Woods in Enniskerry\n\n13 Sika Woods is a beautifully presented three-bedroom semi-detached home situated within the highly sought-after Sika Woods development, just outside the picturesque village of Enniskerry. Built by Winterbrook in 2020 and designed by award-winning Aughney O'Flaherty Architects, this contemporary A-rated residence offers approximately 121 sq m (1,302 sq ft) of thoughtfully designed accommodation, enhanced by a versatile detached Shomra garden room. \n\nPresented in excellent turnkey condition, the property combines striking modern architecture with warm, stylish interiors and enjoys a peaceful setting overlooking landscaped communal areas within this exclusive development of just 47 homes. \n\nUpon entering, a welcoming entrance hall leads to a spacious living room to the front of the property, complete with bespoke built-in cabinetry and shelving, creating an attractive focal point while providing excellent storage. To the rear lies the heart of the home, a stunning open-plan kitchen and dining room featuring impressive double-height ceilings, large picture windows and a beautifully designed kitchen centred around a substantial island unit. Flooded with natural light, this exceptional space is ideal for both everyday family living and entertaining, while sliding doors open directly onto the rear garden. \n\nThe ground floor is further complemented by a utility room and guest WC. \n\nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises three well-proportioned bedrooms and a family bathroom. The principal bedroom enjoys a walk-in wardrobe, stylish ensuite shower room and access to a private balcony. Bedroom two also benefits from direct access to a second balcony overlooking the communal green, while bedroom three provides an ideal children's bedroom, guest room or additional workspace. \n\nA particular feature of this property is the detached Shomra garden room, located within the rear garden. Fully insulated and equipped with power, this versatile space offers endless possibilities and is ideally suited as a home office, gym, playroom, studio or hobby room, providing valuable additional accommodation separate from the main house. \n\nOutside, the rear garden has been thoughtfully landscaped to create a private and low-maintenance outdoor space with patio and lawn areas, ideal for outdoor dining and family enjoyment. To the front, the property benefits from private off-street parking and attractive planting. \n\nSika Woods is located just over one kilometre from the centre of Enniskerry village, one of Wicklow's most desirable locations, renowned for its cafés, restaurants, schools and strong sense of community. The nearby Powerscourt Estate, Wicklow Mountains, Bray seafront and excellent transport connections to Dublin via the M11 and M50 further enhance this exceptional setting. \n\n13 Sika Woods presents a rare opportunity to acquire a stylish, energy-efficient family home in a prestigious development, complete with the added benefit of a fully insulated garden room offering valuable flexible space for modern living. \n\nKey Features \n- Exceptional three-bedroom semi-detached residence extending to approximately 121 sq m / 1,302 sq ft \n- Built in 2020 by Winterbrook and designed by award-winning Aughney O'Flaherty Architects \n- Located within the exclusive Sika Woods development near Enniskerry Village \n- Presented in excellent turnkey condition throughout \n- Stunning open-plan kitchen and dining room with double-height ceilings and feature island unit \n- Spacious living room with bespoke built-in cabinetry and shelving \n- Utility room and guest WC at ground floor level \n- Principal bedroom with walk-in wardrobe, ensuite and private balcony \n- Second bedroom with balcony overlooking landscaped communal green \n- Detached insulated Shomra garden room with power supply, ideal as a home office, gym, playroom or studio \n- Landscaped rear garden with patio and lawn areas \n- Private driveway parking \n- Excellent location convenient to Enniskerry Village, Powerscourt Estate, Bray and Dublin commuter routes"
      },
